  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <h1>Best Notion Alternatives in 2026</h1>
      <div class="meta">Updated July 2026 · Ranked 5 alternatives · Business Tools Pillar · Productivity Category</div>

      <p>Notion is the dominant all-in-one workspace, but it is not the right tool for everyone. Some teams need local-first storage, more powerful formulas, better web clipping, or deeper Microsoft 365 integration. We ranked the five best Notion alternatives in 2026 based on note-taking capability, database features, collaboration, pricing, and how directly each replaces a specific Notion weakness.</p>
      <p>For related comparisons, see <a href="/reviews/notion-vs-obsidian/">Notion vs Obsidian</a>, <a href="/reviews/notion-vs-confluence/">Notion vs Confluence</a>, and <a href="/reviews/notion-vs-evernote/">Notion vs Evernote</a>. Explore the <a href="/reviews/business-tools/">Business Tools Pillar</a> for more productivity and business software reviews.</p>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#quick-comparison">Quick Comparison</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-allinone-clickup">#1 — ClickUp (Best All-in-One Alternative)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-local-obsidian">#2 — Obsidian (Best for Local-First Knowledge Graph)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-interactive-coda">#3 — Coda (Best for Interactive Docs & Formulas)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-capture-evernote">#4 — Evernote (Best for Capture & Web Clipping)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-microsoft-onenote">#5 — Microsoft OneNote (Best for Microsoft 365 Teams)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#selection-scenarios">Selection Scenarios</a></li>
          <li><a href="#buying-guide">Buying Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="quick-comparison">Quick Comparison</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Tool</th>
            <th>Best For</th>
            <th>Starting Price</th>
            <th>Free Tier</th>
            <th>Rating</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>ClickUp</strong></td>
